  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbpedia.org/ontology/PeriodicalLiterature">
    <ns0:comment xml:lang="en">Periodical literature (also called a periodical publication or simply a periodical) is a published work that appears in a new edition on a regular schedule. The most familiar examples are the newspaper, often published daily, or weekly; or the magazine, typically published weekly, monthly or as a quarterly. Other examples would be a newsletter, a literary journal or learned journal, or a yearbook.</ns0:comment>
