  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbpedia.org/ontology/SiteOfSpecialScientificInterest">
    <ns0:comment xml:lang="en">A Site of Special Scientific Interest (SSSI) is a conservation designation denoting a protected area in the United Kingdom. SSSIs are the basic building block of site-based nature conservation legislation and most other legal nature/geological conservation designations in Great Britain are based upon them, including National Nature Reserves, Ramsar Sites, Special Protection Areas, and Special Areas of Conservation.</ns0:comment>
